<title>USA: Telesensory Corp postpones IPO.</title>
<headline>Telesensory Corp postpones IPO.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telesensory Corp has postponed its planned initial public offering, according to underwriter Jefferies &amp; Co.</p>
<p>The company makes braille devices that allow blind people to use personal computers and the Aladdin family of video magnifiers for people with severely impaired vision.</p>
<p>It was not imediately known when the offering would be brought back to market.</p>
